11. What is DDL?
DDL stands for Data Definition Language. 
It is used to create, modify, and delete database objects such as tables and databases


Task 2: Table Modification
Objective: Modify an existing table using DDL commands.
Requirements:
● Add email column with UNIQUE constraint
● Add default value to department
● Drop an unused column

➡️alter table employees
  add email varchar(100);

➡️ALTER TABLE employees
  ADD CONSTRAINT unique_email UNIQUE(email);

➡️insert into employees 
  values(1,'nav',9,'it',50000,'ambati9@gmail.com');  #works well
  
➡️insert into employees 
  values(2,'sai',10,'HR',60000,'ambati9@gmail.com');  #ERROR: 1062 (23000): Duplicate entry 'ambati9@gmail.com' for key 'employees.unique_email'
  
➡️alter table employees
  alter department
  set default 'it';
  
➡️INSERT INTO employees(emp_id,name,age,salary,email)
  VALUES(3,'Sam',11,45000,'sam@gmail.com');
  
➡️alter table employees
  drop column age;
  
➡️desc employees;
  +------------+---------------+------+-----+---------+-------+
  | Field      | Type          | Null | Key | Default | Extra |
  +------------+---------------+------+-----+---------+-------+
